  <ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock id="HHFF9F4E3640A578CDF5DE55A091A9A0F9" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&#xD;
		&lt;div&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;ol type="1" style="margin:0pt; padding-left:0pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;li style="margin-left:31.49pt; padding-left:4.51pt; font-family:Tahoma; font-size:10pt"&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;span&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;/li&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;li style="margin-left:31.49pt; padding-left:4.51pt; font-family:Tahoma; font-size:10pt"&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;span&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;/li&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;li style="margin-left:31.49pt; padding-left:4.51pt; font-family:Tahoma; font-size:10pt"&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;span&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;/li&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;li style="margin-left:31.49pt; padding-left:4.51pt; font-family:Tahoma; font-size:10pt"&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;span&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;/li&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;li style="margin-left:31.49pt; padding-left:4.51pt; font-family:Tahoma; font-size:10pt"&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;span&gt;N/A&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;/li&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/ol&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
		&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;
	&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock>
  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="HHFB845F6A13C048AB10E053139FD9FDD6" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&#xD;
		&lt;div&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-weight:bold"&gt;The Company&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;Dixie Pipeline Company LLC (Dixie), is a Delaware limited liability company and a wholly&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;owned subsidiary of Enterprise Products Operating LLC&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt; (EPOLLC)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;, a Texas limited liability company, and is a consolidated subsidiary of Enterprise Products Partners L.P., a Delaware partnership&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;, which is &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;a publicly traded partnership&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-weight:bold"&gt;Description of the Property&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;Dixie is primarily a propane pipeline system that is approximately 1,300 miles in length. The system extends from southeast Texas and Louisiana to markets in the southeastern United States and the Texas gulf coast. Supplies transported on this system primarily originate from southeast Texas, southern Louisiana and Mississippi. The system operates in seven states: Texas, Louisiana, Mississippi, Alabama, Georgia, South Carolina and North Carolina. Dixie's property, plant and equipment assets are recorded at original cost.&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-weight:bold"&gt;Regulation&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;Dixie is subject to regulation by various federal and state authorities, including the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC).&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-weight:bold"&gt;Basis of Accounting&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;Financial statements are prepared on the accrual basis of accounting. The accounting policies followed in preparation of these financial statements conform to those required by FERC.&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-weight:bold"&gt;Cash and Cash Equivalents&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;Cash equivalents are defined as all highly marketable securities with maturities of three months or less when purchased. The carrying value of cash and cash equivalents approximates fair value because of the short term-to-maturity of these investments. Cash and cash equivalents includes FERC Account 11, Temporary Investments.&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-weight:bold"&gt;Revenue Recognition&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;Dixie's revenues are primarily derived from transportation of propane under tariffs regulated by the FERC. The tariffs specify the amounts to be paid by shippers for service between receipt and delivery locations and the general terms and conditions of transportation services on the pipeline system. Revenues are recorded upon delivery of products to customers.&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-weight:bold"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;Dixie is a limited liability company that passes income tax liability through the company to &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;EPOLLC&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt; and, with the exception of the Texas &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;Franchise&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt; Tax, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;if applicable, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;does not recognize this liability on the company's financial statements. For purposes of calculating income taxes for the annual cost of service (shown on page 700 of the Annual Report), Dixie employs FERC's Policy Statement on Income Tax Allowances.&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-weight:bold"&gt;Employees&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;Dixie has no employees of its own. All operations, management and administrative functions are performed by employees of Enterprise Products Company on behalf of EPOLLC, the operator.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; -aw-import:spaces"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;Dixie reimburses EPOLLC for management and administrative functions under the terms of an &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;operating agreement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
		&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;
	&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfEventsThatHaveAMaterialEffectToRespondentsTextBlock id="HH11476EB422E065C84DE3B12A8533C405" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4"></ferc:DisclosureOfEventsThatHaveAMaterialEffectToRespondentsTextBlock>
